Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:55:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] base: Bypass charging while a game is in front

GameSpace has a bypass charging switch in its panel
(mithermal_bypass_charging) and in its settings
(smart_battery_bypass_charging). While a game is in front and either is
on, set sys.gamespace.bypass_charging=1, which the device's init turns
into a write to the charger node, so the phone runs from the charger
instead of charging the battery.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QY97AsgNLyAwQpzrsxC9zt
---
 .../android/server/wm/GameSpaceService.java   |  1 +
 .../server/wm/GameStateDispatcher.java        | 41 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/GameSpaceService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/GameSpaceService.java
index 9963776d..85483b01 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/GameSpaceService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/GameSpaceService.java
@@ -249,6 +249,7 @@ public final class GameSpaceService extends SystemService {
         mStarted = true;
         mGamePackageHandler.registerPackageReceiver();
         mGameListManager.registerGameListObserver(mHandler);
+        mGameStateDispatcher.observeBypassCharging(mHandler);
